-- statement:
--   For countably many positive compact C1 source bands, each with its own explicit genuine Lipschitz and bounded-value estimates, one single full-measure set of original BV Lévy and dividend paths identifies all original global marked NX signed nonlinear C1 integrals with their actual stopped negative-jump-time positive-minus-negative series, for every finite ruin/horizon clock. This source-exact proof combines accepted physical NX integrability, accepted original jump-time signed real source identity, and the pinned Mathlib countable almost-everywhere equivalence. It directly aligns every localisation band of the original compensated HJB certificate with the real raw-jump-time summation on the exact same stopped original Lévy sample path, including final contact and excluding zero.

